@startuml review_report_02_chunked_report
' Review unit 02 of 02 -- see docs/review_report.md for the series.
' State AFTER commit 4998269 (src +178/-5, tests +40, docs +3/-1).
' Every number below is from a run of the cases at commit 4998269.
' Render: plantuml docs/review_report_02_chunked_report.puml

title Unit 02 -- the report on the chunked path, measured in the workers (a786b4a..4998269)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Monospaced
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ArrowColor #555555
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #FCFCFC
  BorderColor #777777
  DiamondBackgroundColor #F2F2F2
  DiamondBorderColor #777777
}
skinparam partition {
  BorderColor #8899AA
  FontColor #33495E
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFDF0
  BorderColor #C8C08A
}

start

partition "the call -- unchanged" {
  :<b>case B</b>: the unit-00 call with max_obs=40 -> NTASKS 3, merge_nc=True;
}

partition "validate, configure -- unchanged" {
  :self._requested stored, num_obs 102, var_num_obs 102 and 26, dim_split 1;
}

partition "workers/generate_chunk  (one process per chunk)" {
  :place this chunk's strata, VariableEncoding.to_stored;
  #C8E6C9:measurements = <b>GenerationReport.measure_chunk</b>(
     records, var_dims_indices, dim_split, task_range[0])
  per variable: occupied count, one used-coordinate vector per axis
  per non-reference variable: |a & b| and |a| on the shared dims;
  note right #C8E6C9
    Plain ints and short lists, picklable.
    Taken before the records are released,
    so nothing is read back from disk.
  end note
  :write the chunk netCDF and parquet, as before;
  #C8E6C9:return (chunk_id, total_obs, parquet_chunk_path, <b>measurements</b>);
  #FFCDD2:return (chunk_id, total_obs, parquet_chunk_path);
}

partition "GenerateData._generate_par" {
  #C8E6C9:chunk_summaries.append(measurements) for each finished chunk;
  #C8E6C9:<b>GenerationReport.from_chunks</b>(self, chunk_summaries)
  observations, intersections, reference projections: summed
  (overlap never spans strata, so the counts add up)
  coverage: OR of the axis vectors, the split axis placed by offset
  density: occupied / prod(gen.shape), the FULL grid;
  :consolidate parquet, merge netCDF, return (None, None) as before;
}

#FFF9C4:<b>case B</b>, parallel, printed at the end of the run
  ~ num_obs              requested 100    got 102
    observations var0    requested 102    got 102
  ! density      var0    requested 0.4    got 0.398438
    coverage     var0    yes
    observations var1    requested 26     got 26
  ! density      var1    requested 0.1    got <b>0.101562</b> (full grid)
  ! coverage     var1    got <b>unused on x0</b>
  ! overlap F1   var1    requested 0.5    got 0.45614
  4 of 8 differ (no "values in parquet" rows: there is no DataFrame);

#FFF9C4:<b>serial vs parallel, the same data</b> --
                serial (unit 01)    parallel (unit 02)
density var1    0.40625             0.101562
coverage var1   yes                 unused on x0
overlap F1      0.45614             0.45614
case S:  density var1 1.0 serial, 0.25 parallel; coverage as above;

:<b>netCDF and parquet unchanged</b>: every case writes the same files
as units 00 and 01, and serial equals parallel;

stop

legend right
  |<#C8E6C9> green |= added or changed by THIS unit |
  |<#FFCDD2> red |= removed by THIS unit |
  |<#FFE0B2> orange |= single-variable flow touched by THIS unit |
  |<#FFF9C4> yellow |= generated data or file that changed as a result |
  | plain | unchanged since unit 01 |

  <b>What to review in unit 02</b>
  * the summing argument: occupancy and intersections add
    across chunks because overlap never spans strata
  * measure_chunk takes the chunk records, which keep every
    dimension (constant dims unsqueezed). var1 is pinned to one
    x0 coordinate, so its x0 vector is mostly False and the
    report says "unused on x0". Serial measures the squeezed
    array and says "yes".
  * density divides by the full grid here and by the
    variable's own grid in from_arrays: the two paths disagree
    for any variable that drops a dimension.
  * the test that pins serial = parallel uses variables on every
    dimension, so it does not see either difference.
  <b>Verified</b>: output files unchanged; 548 tests pass.
  The two disagreements are in the original 5e31df1 as well.
end legend

@enduml
